  "description": "Fuji makes Finest frames in\n\ntwo materials, aluminum and steel, and seven sizes. The 7005-Series butted\n\naluminum-framed model is called the Finest-AL. The frame features double water\n\nbottle mounts. The rear derailleur hanger unbolts so you can replace it if\n\nit's bent or broken from a tumble or clumsy baggage handling.\n\nLike the steel version, Finest-AL uses a butted, tapered, aero-shaped Cro-Moly\n\nsteel fork.\n\nThe equipment is all good, solid stuff, mostly Shimano Sora. Three chainrings,\n\nlots of gears, not much weight, tons of versatility. Dual-Pivot brakes; Sturdy stainless steel spokes, 32 per\n\nwheel; sealed, low-maintenance bottom bracket. If I rode club rides on weekends\n\nand those rides got more competitive than I might like, I'd buy a Finest-AL.\n\nIf it's not technically \"faster\" than a steel Finest, it feels quicker,\n\nlike a racing bicycle. I'd feel quicker, like a bicycle racer.",
